{
 "0001": {
  "title": "",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_01\" id=\"tag_17_533_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "setsockopt — set the socket options",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_02\" id=\"tag_17_533_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">sys/socket.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint setsockopt(int</tt> <i>socket</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>level</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>option_name</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; const void *</tt><i>option_value</i><tt>, socklen_t</tt> <i>option_len</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_03\" id=\"tag_17_533_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]setsockopt[/I5]() function shall set the option specified by the [I6]option_name[/I6] argument, at the protocol level\nspecified by the [I7]level[/I7] argument, to the value pointed to by the [I8]option_value[/I8] argument for the socket associated with\nthe file descriptor specified by the [I9]socket[/I9] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I10]level[/I10] argument specifies the protocol level at which the option resides. To set options at the socket level, specify\nthe [I11]level[/I11] argument as SOL_SOCKET. To set options at other levels, supply the appropriate [I12]level[/I12] identifier for the\nprotocol controlling the option. For example, to indicate that an option is interpreted by the TCP (Transport Control Protocol),\nset [I13]level[/I13] to IPPROTO_TCP as defined in the [A14][I15]&lt;netinet/in.h&gt;[/I15][/A14]\nheader.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A14": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/netinet_in.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I16]option_name[/I16] argument specifies a single option to set. It can be one of the socket-level options defined in [A17][I18]&lt;sys/socket.h&gt;[/I18][/A17] and described in [A19][I20]2.10.16 Use of Options[/I20][/A19]. If [I21]option_name[/I21] is equal to SO_RCVTIMEO or\nSO_SNDTIMEO and the implementation supports setting the option, it is unspecified whether the [B22]struct timeval[/B22] pointed to by\n[I23]option_value[/I23] is stored as provided by this function or is rounded up to align with the resolution of the clock being used.\nIf [I24]setsockopt[/I24]() is called with [I25]option_name[/I25] equal to SO_ACCEPTCONN, SO_ERROR, or SO_TYPE, the behavior is\nunspecified.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A17": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A19": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/V2_chap02.html#tag_16_10_16\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I21": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B22": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00009",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A26][/A26]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A26": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_04\" id=\"tag_17_533_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I27]setsockopt[/I27]() shall return 0. Otherwise, -1 shall be returned and [I28]errno[/I28] set to indicate\nthe error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00011",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A29][/A29]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A29": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_05\" id=\"tag_17_533_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I30]setsockopt[/I30]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00013",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EBADF]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00014",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I31]socket[/I31] argument is not a valid file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00015",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EDOM]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00016",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The send and receive timeout values are too big to fit into the timeout fields in the socket structure.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00017",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00018",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The specified option is invalid at the specified socket level or the socket has been shut down.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00019",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EISCONN]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00020",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The socket is already connected, and a specified option cannot be set while the socket is connected.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00021",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[ENOPROTOOPT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00022",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The option is not supported by the protocol.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00023",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[ENOTSOCK]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00024",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     25
    ],
    "text": "The [I32]socket[/I32] argument does not refer to a socket.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00025",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I33]setsockopt[/I33]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00026",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[ENOMEM]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00027",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     5
    ],
    "text": "There was insufficient memory available for the operation to complete.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00028",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[ENOBUFS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00029",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Insufficient resources are available in the system to complete the call.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00030",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A34][/A34]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_06\" id=\"tag_17_533_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00031",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00032",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A35][/A35]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A35": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_533_07\" id=\"tag_17_533_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00033",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I36]setsockopt[/I36]() function provides an application program with the means to control socket behavior. An application\nprogram can use [I37]setsockopt[/I37]() to allocate buffer space, control timeouts, or permit socket data broadcasts. The [A38][I39]&lt;sys/socket.h&gt;[/I39][/A38] header defines the socket-level options available to\n[I40]setsockopt[/I40]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A38": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00034",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Options may exist at multiple protocol levels. The SO_ options are always present at the uppermost socket level.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00035",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     5
    ],
    "text": "It is implementation-defined which socket options, if any, are inherited from a listening socket to an accepted socket by\n[A41][I42]accept[/I42]()[/A41] or [A43][I44]accept4[/I44]()[/A43].",
    "placeholders": {
     "A41": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/accept.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I42": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A43": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/accept4.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00036",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43
    ],
